  "localAdaptations": [
    "main.cpp keeps the independent scenario block-dump streams (a child scenario that names the boot capture path is refused; one that names another path writes its own) and the per-child audio-capture flag, as the 7b2984c8 import did.",
    "test_periph.cpp keeps the injected media-exhaustion case for --card-fail-after ahead of upstream's unplug/plug case.",
    "The Makefile keeps every Modwerk adaptation of the 7b2984c8 import (OCTABAM_STATIC_STOCK=1 exported, the approved stock mailbox, the local gate set) and adds only the setup-linux and setup-mac entry points; nothing else of upstream's current Makefile is taken.",
    "docs/TRAPS.md and docs/remixer/EMU.md are upstream's docs/contributing/TRAPS.md and tools/emu/README.md unchanged; their relative links name octabam's own tree. sdk/octabam/AGENTS.md stays at its 30 September 2026 text.",
    "The two DSP source gates are not wired into the vendored build_bus.py (a builder input pinned by sdk/infrastructure-verification/); scripts/dsp-source-gates.py runs them over every module, platform and base source from modules:check and module:doctor, refusing a label prefix always and a rep in modules listed from 2026-10-23."
  ],
  "verificationRecord": "infrastructure-verification/octabam-emulator-gates-5c71bc8c.json",
  "limitations": [
    "The emulator core (v4e, dsp, periph, card) is byte-identical to upstream before and after; only the bench protocol, scripting, write watches and stall detection changed. Firmware-free unit tests and a compile are the evidence: no boot of a stock image, no hardware.",
    "No builder file (build_bus.py, ab_image.py, schema.py, platform_build.py, ledger.py) changed, so every image and refusal of the 7b2984c8 record is reproduced by identity, not by a fresh native build."
  ]
